+# Dormant adaptive-media foundation
+
+Not connected to SourceBuffer, HTMLMediaElement or NDK decoders yet. Does not enable MSE support or change capability reporting. Existing DOM drafts040/041 must stay excluded from candidates.
+
+Dependency pinned to shiguredo_mp4=2026.5.0, Apache-2.0. Actual Servo toolchain1.99.1 meets its Rust1.93 requirement; this raises the experimental backend dependency's effective MSRV, not Servo's whole-workspace manifest promise. Registry checksum82e773aead88d11a806c8b78dbc2577afb3a20fcc80108aafb3724f6dbb9fbe0, source commit30e9b347f8863cd7d377e728ca7a81ac5a1b7770.
+
+Implemented incremental bounded box framing, transactional fMP4 sample extraction, signed timestamp conversion, sample bounds against original mdat payloads, raw trun count preflight before allocation. Multiple mdat/ignored boxes handled with byte-position-preserving parser envelope; returned samples must lie wholly in one ORIGINAL mdat payload. Coded-frame storage has byte quota, offset/window handling, random-access gating, overlap/dependent-frame removal and per-track ranges. AVC SPS/PPS CSD and length-prefix to AnnexB conversion prepared for Android decoder input.
+
+Not complete MSE: missing DOM event/state/object identity integration, native decoder bridge, source-buffer attachment/delivery, full coded-frame processing semantics (sequence mode, discontinuity detection, multiplexed-track range intersection, eviction), edit-list support, brand compatibility, WebM, and full parser security/resource review. Unsupported edits/DRM are rejected. Do not advertise codecs based solely on this parser.
+
+Host evidence: existing57 tests plus18 new checks (13 unit +5 fixture integration) pass. Fixture is a locally generated32x32 blue AVC fMP4 with2 frames, no user media. It demonstrates parsing, not codec playback. Generated using ffmpeg lavfi color blue/2fps/1s, libx264 ultrafast/g1, empty_moov+frag_keyframe+default_base_moof. Primary requirements: https://www.w3.org/TR/mse-byte-stream-format-isobmff/ and https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaCodec (CSD section).
